<title>MEXICO: Mexico heavy vehicle sales soar in May-industry.</title>
<headline>Mexico heavy vehicle sales soar in May-industry.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico notched up 1,324 heavy vehicle sales in May, an increase of 141 percent from year-ago levels, the National Association of Heavy Vehicle Producers (ANPACT) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>An ANPACT statement said heavy vehicle sales for the year to date totalled 5,437 units, up 117 percent from the same period last year.</p>
<p>The breakdown of heavy vehicle sales in May was as follows:</p>
<p>Product			Units Sold	Pct Change vs May 96</p>
<p>Heavy trucks			  524		  97.74 pct</p>
<p>Chassis				 287		 208.60 pct</p>
<p>Five-axle trucks		    434		 309.43 pct</p>
<p>Construction vehicles		 3		 200.00 pct</p>
<p>Buses				    76		  -8.43 pct</p>
<p>(( --Veronica Galan, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9553))</p>
</text>
